[center][size=6][b]Taoist[/b][/size]
[i]A hardcore overhaul of Tale of Immortal (鬼谷八荒) with a living world, a harsh economy, towns you can rule, families and storylines, new paths of cultivation, houses of your own, cultivator clans with their elders, and tougher battles.[/i]

[url=https://github.com/4azuo/GuiGuBaHuang-Taoist][b]GitHub[/b][/url]  •  [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3161035078][b]Steam Workshop[/b][/url]  •  [url=https://github.com/4azuo/GuiGuBaHuang-Taoist/issues/13][b]Report a Bug[/b][/url]  •  [url=https://discord.gg/XKaP3EYfw][b]Discord[/b][/url]  •  [url=https://ko-fi.com/fouru][b]Support on Ko-fi[/b][/url][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b]📥Download[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Taoist:[/b]  [url=https://github.com/4azuo/GuiGuBaHuang-Taoist/releases]Direct[/url] | [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3161035078]Steam Workshop[/url] [/*]
[*][b]Fouru's ModLib v2.3.00 or newer (required):[/b]  [url=https://github.com/4azuo/GuiGuBaHuang-Taoist/releases]Direct[/url] | [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3385996759]Steam Workshop[/url] [/*]
[*][b]ModLib must be at the TOP of your mod load order.[/b] Restart the game after you change the order. [/*]
[/list][size=5][b]⚙ Configuration[/b][/size]
You can tune or turn off most features in [b]S&M Configs[/b] on the title screen. Optional features are on [b]page 3[/b], the storylines on [b]page 4[/b], the options of other mods (Dao of Creation) on the pages after. The harder your settings, the higher your [b]S&M score[/b] and the better your rewards.
You can change in-game options such as notifications, encounters and artifact hotkeys under [b]Settings → Taoist Settings[/b].

[line]

[size=5][b]★ What's New in 6.2 (v6.2.0)[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]Choose Your Destinies[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Character creation has a new window with [b]every innate destiny of the game[/b], sorted by quality and name, with filters by quality, name and description[/*]
[*]Take as many as you like, on top of the 3 you roll. Each one lowers the S&M score of the new save (3,000 to 8,000 P by quality)[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Taoist × Dao of Creation[/b][/size]
Optional: only when you play both mods. Taoist runs as before without it.
[list]
[*]2 new storylines: [i]The Nameless Art[/i] (an outcast invents a martial art, and the old sect wants it) and [i]For One Heir Only[/i] (a dying master, one last art, two candidates)[/*]
[*]Characters create martial arts of their own and teach them to you, and 9 endings of the older storylines reward you with an art or Dao Essence[/*]
[*]The options of Dao of Creation have their own page in S&M Configs[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Also New[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Taoist wallpapers for the title screen (Change Theme)[/*]
[*]Trainer: teleport by area (choose an area, then a place)[/*]
[*]The windows of several mods (notices, error reports consent) no longer open over each other[/*]
[/list]
[size=5][b]What's New in 6.1[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]Clan Elders[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Outsiders of no kin who guard a clan: their realm follows the area, their number the clan's house. They are paid a monthly salary and a yearly offering[/*]
[*]They have no say in the clan's affairs, but they [b]vote on its wars[/b] (the head has 3 votes) and fight in them[/*]
[*]Invite elders to your own clan, become the guardian elder of an NPC clan that trusts you, or resign. Declare war through the war council[/*]
[*]In a clan war the elders fight beside their clan in the real battle. A disloyal elder may flee, or even [b]betray its clan mid-battle[/b], and is hunted down afterwards[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Succession[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]When the head of a clan dies, a son or daughter takes over (else a grandchild, a brother or sister, or the spouse). Play on as your child and you may head the clan yourself[/*]
[*]A clan wiped out leaves its [b]mansion in ruins[/b]: another clan may take it as its seat, or it is split into plots for the mortals[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Also New[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Faster months: the NPCs grow by turns (S&M GrowUpSpeed), and the game saves in the background (ModLib 2.2.36)[/*]
[*]S&M score balance: growth speed, NPC count, monsters, level-up exp, bank fees and taxes on one scale[/*]
[*]New windows for the plots, the clans and the elders (cards with portraits and pictures)[/*]
[*]Taoist Settings: an option to hide the [i]Damage Calc[/i] button of the battle screen (F9 still opens the window)[/*]
[/list]
[size=5][b]What's New in 6.0[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]Five New Paths of Cultivation[/b][/size]
Each path has its own button on the cultivation screen and can be turned off in S&M Configs.
[list]
[*][b]Body Refining:[/b] Copper Skin → Iron Bone → Jade Marrow → Golden Body → Undying Body. Temper your flesh with the blows you take, training and medicinal baths for max HP, defense and fist / palm / finger. Train under waterfalls, in lava pools and thunder pools, and face the [b]body tribulation[/b] at each bottleneck. Some sects teach it, and NPCs walk the path too[/*]
[*][b]Merit & Karma:[/b] good deeds bring attack, defense, luck, gifts from the grateful, friendlier NPCs and softer lightning. Evil deeds bring more attack but less defense, bounties and revenge. With enough karma you can [b]massacre a town[/b] in a real battle and leave it in ruins for 10 years[/*]
[*][b]Artisan Dao:[/b] alchemy, forging, talismans, feng shui, herbs and mining as 6 crafts with ranks, guild exams, masterpieces, NPC commissions and apprentices. Every area has [b]mine veins[/b] and [b]herb valleys[/b] where you can stay for years[/*]
[*][b]Dao Heart:[/b] the steadiness of your mind. Raises max SP / MP and your odds against heart demons. Betrayal and broken promises shake it[/*]
[*][b]Spirit Sense:[/b] raises max SP, senses ambushes and keeps heart demons away. Once a month, [b]scan[/b] your surroundings: the cultivators around you (portraits, the hostile ones first), herbs, ores and the nearest places[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Estates[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Every town has its own map of plots in districts, with mortals who live and grow and a palace for the town master[/*]
[*]Buy land or a mortal's house, and build it up from a [i]Thatched Hut[/i] to an [i]Immortal Palace[/i][/*]
[*]Rooms: quiet room, training ground, herb garden, spirit gathering array, ancestral hall[/*]
[*]Pay the house tax every month or the house is taken back. NPCs buy houses too, and families live together[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Also New[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]4 new storylines: [i]Old Tie's Forge, The House on the Old Street, Ashes of the Town, A Heartbeat in the Stone[/i][/*]
[*]S&M Configs: options for the new paths and estates (on/off, gain rates, prices, tax), storylines on a page of their own[/*]
[*]The Rebirth button is now in the player info. Many fixes[/*]
[/list]
[line]

[size=5][b]✦ Features[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]New Game[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Pick starting divine artifacts at character creation (Bagua Jade, Eye of Providence, Devil Demon Pot, in any combination)[/*]
[*]Option to skip the intro and the first battle[/*]
[*]Character and NPC roles: [b]Power, Speed, Tao, Atk, Def, Angel, Evil, Merchant[/b], each with its own advantages[/*]
[*]Destiny level priority, S&M difficulty presets (Level 0-10), [b]one-life mode[/b] and a built-in trainer[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]S&M Score[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Every S&M setting is worth points: harder settings raise the score, easier ones lower it[/*]
[*]The score changes battle exp and loot (-20% to +50%), and gives a title and a start bonus for a new save[/*]
[*]Score records of every character across your saves[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Living World & NPCs[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]NPCs grow, level up their skills, craft artifacts, and earn roles and titles[/*]
[*][b]Teams:[/b] hire NPCs for a monthly wage, or recruit friends for free. Members grow closer by fighting beside you, but some may betray you[/*]
[*]NPCs join battles as enemies, allies, sect members or town guards[/*]
[*][b]Stalkers[/b] follow you after you show rare items. Fight them or pay them off[/*]
[*][b]Random encounters[/b] with choices and rewards: wounded cultivator, chess hermit, hooded peddler, collapsed cave, spirit beast cub, town festival, and a rare heavenly trial[/*]
[*]Reworked dramas and quests (slice-of-life, challenge master, item commissions)[/*]
[*]NPCs sometimes find their own fortunes and ancient inheritances[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Storylines[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]16 NPC storylines[/b] with portraits, real battles, a drawn scene for every step, and a quest in the Mission window[/*]
[*]Multi-act lines with time limits and failure branches that lead to alternate paths. The lines remember how the others ended[/*]
[*]Includes [i]Cold Sword, Old Huang's Debt, Exploding Furnace, Sworn Brothers, Granny's Herb Garden[/i], the finale [i]Red Lotus[/i], the long lines [i]Hundred-Year Wager[/i] and [i]Roadside Inn[/i] (over a hundred years each), and [i]Sealed Tomb, Cursed Disciple, Thunder Remnant, Heart Demon[/i] at higher realms[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Families & Legacy[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]NPCs take dao companions (same-sex option available) and have children, who join the world at age 16[/*]
[*]Your household: monthly upkeep, gifts from your family, a family accounts window, and your family tree on the kinship screen. Families avenge their fallen members[/*]
[*][b]Legacy play:[/b] when your character dies, continue as your child or grandchild and keep your items, spirit stones and techniques (S&M option)[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Economy[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Inflation and currency reform, with sales and price-hike events every June and December[/*]
[*]A percentage surcharge on buying and selling in towns[/*]
[*][b]Banking:[/b] opening an account costs money, storage has monthly fees, and storage locks if you don't pay[/*]
[*][b]Loans:[/b] 3% interest per month, due in 12 months. Overdue debts bring reminder letters, then debt collectors. Defeat them twice and the bank writes off the debt but blacklists you[/*]
[*][b]Player market:[/b] list items, negotiate in spirit stones or by barter, use the VIP market, see recent deal prices and post buy orders filled by the townspeople[/*]
[*]Exchange items for sect contribution points[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Towns & Warfare[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Become a town master or guardian: manage the budget, tax rate and buildings, and upgrade your town into a city[/*]
[*]Declare war on other towns and defend against [b]monster waves[/b]. You are called back if your town is attacked[/*]
[*][b]Cultivator clans[/b] in every town: relations, alliances, brawls, blood feuds and clan wars, with elders who guard them[/*]
[*][b]Bounties:[/b] town masters post wanted notices and hunters chase the targets, including you. You can also hunt targets yourself from the bounty board[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Cultivation[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Seclusion and enlightenment can last for years (spirit veins, inheritances, heart demons, time rifts) while the world keeps moving[/*]
[*]Qi cultivation, spirit stone cultivation and natural breakthroughs[/*]
[*]More exp needed to level up. [b]Rebirth[/b] to level 1 to cultivate again with better base stats[/*]
[*]Time skips simulate every month of the world, with a progress window[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Battle & Growth[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Mana shields[/b] for players, NPCs and monsters, plus special monsters that grow stronger[/*]
[*]Reworked damage and defense with block, evade and crit rules[/*]
[*][b]Damage Calc[/b] window (battle button, player info or F9): your attack and defense step by step, the last hits dealt and taken, and the last foes compared with you[/*]
[*]Stats grow through battle. Skills and artifacts gain expertise[/*]
[*][b]Losing a battle has a price:[/b] exp, items, spirit stones, lifespan, or your character in one-life mode. The [i]Resurrection Pill[/i] and rings offer protection[/*]
[*]Custom refining for rings, outfits, artifacts and mounts, with random stat slots by rarity. Slot [i]n[/i] unlocks at refine level [i]n × 100[/i], and unlocked slots can be rerolled[/*]
[*]Use several divine artifacts at once, each with its own hotkey, and repair damaged ones[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Interface[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Taoist Log:[/b] a month-by-month record of taxes, fees, deals, loans, bounties and encounters[/*]
[*]Icons for spirit stones, stats and items in the mod's texts[/*]
[*]Optional: hide the battle map and unit count, and hide training and skill previews[/*]
[*]Languages: [b]English, Chinese (Simplified and Traditional), Korean, Japanese, Vietnamese, Thai, Russian, German, French, Spanish, Latin[/b], plus a custom language system[/*]
[/list][i]...and much more. See the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3161035078]Steam Workshop page[/url] for the full changelog.[/i]

[line]

[size=5][b]📥 Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [b]Fouru's ModLib[/b] v2.3.00 or newer (link above).[/*]
[*]Download [b]Taoist[/b] from the [b]Files[/b] tab, or [url=https://github.com/4azuo/GuiGuBaHuang-Taoist/releases]here[/url].[/*]
[*]Put both mods in your game's mod folder.[/*]
[*]Launch the game, move [b]ModLib to the top[/b] of the mod list, then [b]restart[/b] the game.[/*]
[/list][i]Steam users can simply subscribe on the Workshop.[/i]

[size=5][b]🐞 Bug Reports & Support[/b][/size]
Please read the [url=https://github.com/4azuo/GuiGuBaHuang-Taoist/issues/15]FAQ[/url] first. To report a bug, post in [b]#taoist-bug-reports[/b] on the [url=https://discord.gg/XKaP3EYfw]Discord server[/url] (or the [url=https://github.com/4azuo/GuiGuBaHuang-Taoist/issues/13]Taoist issue thread[/url]) and attach:
[list]
[*]The latest log files:
[code]C:\Users\<YourName>\AppData\LocalLow\guigugame\guigubahuang\mod\flQrxq[/code][/*]
[*]Your save file (export it from the main menu)[/*]
[*]Your mod folder:
[code]C:\Users\<YourName>\AppData\LocalLow\guigugame\guigubahuang\mod[/code][/*]
[/list][line]

